1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,970
Almost there. You're doing great.

2
00:00:05,970 --> 00:00:07,570
Thanks for lifting my spirits.

3
00:00:07,570 --> 00:00:09,970
Next time, try lifting the box.

4
00:00:10,790 --> 00:00:12,270
Please hurry

5
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:14,110
I don't need a treadmill!

6
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:16,860
The doctor says you need to get exercise!

7
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:19,210
I get plenty of exercise!

8
00:00:19,210 --> 00:00:22,640
Crushing my will to live isn't exercise!

9
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:26,000
If she isn't gonna use it, then why are we doing this?

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:26,960
She'll use it.

11
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:29,140
All I need is to rig it

12
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:31,090
with a fishing pole and a HoneyBaked Ham.

13
00:00:31,450 --> 00:00:32,540
All right.

14
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:34,020
Now what?

15
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:35,790
We set it up in Howie's old room.

16
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:37,130
Do you know how to set it up?

17
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:39,530
Please, I'm an MIT-trained engineer.

18
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:40,760
I think I can handle...

19
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,060
Ma, look out!

20
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:48,560
I told you this thing would kill me!

21
00:01:14,610 --> 00:01:17,870
So she's gonna be laid up for at least six weeks.

22
00:01:17,870 --> 00:01:19,490
Poor Mrs. Wolowitz.

23
00:01:19,490 --> 00:01:21,250
Should we do something for her?

24
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,470
I know.

25
00:01:22,470 --> 00:01:25,050
Let's go see the new Spider-Man movie.

26
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:28,350
Sheldon, we're talking about your friend's mother.

27
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:29,670
She got hurt.

28
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:31,660
I thought that subject had run its course,

29
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:33,420
so I changed it.

30
00:01:33,420 --> 00:01:35,800
It's called reading the room, Amy.

31
00:01:37,350 --> 00:01:38,110
Hi.

32
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:39,490
Hey, how were things on the set?

33
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:40,910
Uh, pretty good, actually.

34
00:01:40,910 --> 00:01:42,660
So the movie's not as bad as you thought?

35
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:43,800
Oh, no, it is,

36
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:45,680
but I decided, instead of complaining about it,

37
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,910
I'm just gonna go in every day and give it my all.

38
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:49,230
- Good for you. - Thanks.

39
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:50,670
There's no reason why I shouldn't be

40
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:53,650
the best bisexual go-go dancer slowly transforming

41
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:56,890
into a killer gorilla anyone's ever seen.

42
00:01:57,930 --> 00:01:58,640
I don't know.

43
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,060
The bisexual gorilla go-go dancer in Schindler's List

44
00:02:01,060 --> 00:02:02,930
is tough to beat.

45
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,530
Ah, very good.

46
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:07,640
Because a gorilla go-go dancer of any sexual preference

47
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,760
would be out of place in a film about the Holocaust.

48
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:14,470
It only gets funnier when you explain it, Sheldon.

49
00:02:14,810 --> 00:02:16,460
I know.

50
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:23,800
Okay, she's all settled in the guest room.

51
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:25,200
Maybe we should get one of those machines

52
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,980
to help her up the stairs.

53
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:29,020
You mean a forklift?

54
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,580
- Howie... - I'm sorry.

55
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:33,560
I just can't deal with this right now.

56
00:02:33,560 --> 00:02:35,930
Taking care of your own mother? How can you say that?

57
00:02:35,930 --> 00:02:38,640
Bernie, she's gonna be off her feet for six to eight weeks.

58
00:02:38,640 --> 00:02:41,240
Are you prepared to feed her, wash her

59
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,900
and take her to the toilet?

60
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:46,130
- I would do it for my mother. - Yeah, of course you would--

61
00:02:46,130 --> 00:02:48,010
you're a loving person.

62
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:51,450
I'm what my people would call a putz.

63
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,090
Look, I'm not crazy about the idea,

64
00:02:55,090 --> 00:02:56,740
but what other choice do we have?

65
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:57,920
We get a nurse.

66
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,880
Preferably someone from a Third World country

67
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:03,300
who's used to suffering and unpleasant smells.

68
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,910
You'd hire a total stranger

69
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:08,550
to take care of the woman who raised you?

70
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:09,730
That's so cruel.

71
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:11,890
Not if we pay them well

72
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:15,080
and let them listen to the music of their homeland.

73
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:19,180
I need to tinkle!

74
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:21,760
Sounds like a job for a loving person.

75
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:24,890
Would you like me to play some Polish music

76
00:03:24,890 --> 00:03:27,310
while you carry her to the toilet?

77
00:03:28,310 --> 00:03:30,600
You are a putz.

78
00:03:31,950 --> 00:03:33,780
As advertised.

79
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:38,950
Thanks for coming with me.

80
00:03:38,950 --> 00:03:41,860
Thanks for inviting me after everyone else said no.

81
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:45,580
Aren't you gonna get 3-D glasses?

82
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,100
I brought my own.

83
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:51,010
No sense in risking bridge-of-nose herpes.

84
00:03:52,630 --> 00:03:54,010
Is that a real thing?

85
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:56,920
Well, until they invent nose condoms,

86
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,720
I'm not finding out.

87
00:04:00,550 --> 00:04:02,470
Emily! Hey!

88
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:04,160
Oh, hey, Raj.

89
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,340
Uh, this is my friend, Sheldon.

90
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:07,380
Sheldon, this is Emily.

91
00:04:07,380 --> 00:04:10,320
Oh, yes, you're the dermatologist.

92
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:14,400
I went for a walk yesterday without sunscreen.

93
00:04:15,150 --> 00:04:17,880
Do you see anything on my forehead

94
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:21,420
that I should be concerned about?

95
00:04:21,550 --> 00:04:23,680
Um, you know what? I better go.

96
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:25,190
My movie's about to start.

97
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:26,280
Are you here alone?

98
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,470
No, not really.

99
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:28,500
What do you mean, "not really"?

100
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,990
- Hey, should we get our seats? - Yeah.

101
00:04:30,990 --> 00:04:33,880
It was nice seeing you. Um, I'll call you later.

102
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,400
Yeah, okay.

103
00:04:38,610 --> 00:04:40,840
That was awkward, right?

104
00:04:43,570 --> 00:04:44,980
Is it because she's dating you

105
00:04:44,980 --> 00:04:46,840
but was out with that other fellow?

106
00:04:46,840 --> 00:04:47,520
Yes.

107
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:50,540
Good. I thought she saw something on my forehead.

108
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:55,550
And... action.

109
00:04:55,550 --> 00:04:57,490
Please don't shut me out.

110
00:04:57,490 --> 00:04:58,990
Go away.

111
00:04:58,990 --> 00:05:01,360
Just go away.

112
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,710
I swear, I will find a way to turn you back.

113
00:05:04,710 --> 00:05:05,960
What gave you the right

114
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:09,500
to mix my DNA with that of a killer gorilla?

115
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:12,680
I was trying to save your life.

116
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:15,770
Life? What life? Look at me! I'm a monster!

117
00:05:15,770 --> 00:05:17,470
And now I have blood on my hands, or

118
00:05:17,470 --> 00:05:19,690
paws. I don't know.

119
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:26,660
You can't give up. I love you.

120
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,680
I love you, too.

121
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:33,050
But I'm afraid I love killing more.

122
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:35,910
Like, one day, I might actually try and kill you!

123
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:41,820
And... cut. All right.

124
00:05:44,490 --> 00:05:46,360
All right, let's set up for the next scene.

125
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:48,840
Actually, you know what? Can we do one more?

126
00:05:49,770 --> 00:05:51,270
I think I could do it better.

127
00:05:51,270 --> 00:05:52,280
Let's just move on.

128
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,760
- No one cares. - Well, I care.

129
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,400
I mean, look, if we're gonna do this,

130
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:58,460
why not try and make it something we're actually proud of?

131
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:02,520
Look, sweetie,

132
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:03,760
this movie is garbage,

133
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:05,290
but you should be happy about that,

134
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:08,980
'cause if it was a good movie, you wouldn't be in it.

135
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:10,270
Whoa, whoa, hang on.

136
00:06:10,270 --> 00:06:11,860
There's no need to insult her.

137
00:06:11,860 --> 00:06:12,670
And who are you?

138
00:06:12,670 --> 00:06:13,860
I'm her boyfriend.

139
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:15,250
Isn't she too hot for you?

140
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,700
A little, yeah.

141
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:19,340
Well, boyfriend, get off my set.

142
00:06:19,340 --> 00:06:20,480
You can't do that. He's with me.

143
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,260
You know what? You can get off my set, too.

144
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:22,900
You're fired.

145
00:06:22,900 --> 00:06:24,950
What? You can't fire me. I'm the star.

146
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:28,520
I'm the girl that goes bananas. It says so on the poster.

147
00:06:29,150 --> 00:06:31,660
Yeah, but we just shot the last scene where we see your face.

148
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:36,470
So from now own, the star of the movie is whoever wears this.

149
00:06:38,090 --> 00:06:40,000
Hey, if you're gonna fire her,

150
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,910
then you have to fire me, too.

151
00:06:42,210 --> 00:06:46,060
Wow, that fell apart really fast.

152
00:06:50,930 --> 00:06:52,580
Thanks for skipping the movie.

153
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,460
I couldn't sit in that theater for two hours

154
00:06:54,460 --> 00:06:56,810
wondering about Emily and that guy.

155
00:06:56,810 --> 00:06:58,460
Oh, quite all right.

156
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,510
After my forehead melanoma scare,

157
00:07:00,510 --> 00:07:02,930
I've learned not to sweat the small stuff.

158
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:06,170
Well, sorry,

159
00:07:06,170 --> 00:07:09,140
I don't have all the ingredients to make chai tea.

160
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,350
You don't have to make me anything.

161
00:07:10,350 --> 00:07:12,760
No, I do. You're upset about Emily

162
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:13,560
and you're Indian.

163
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:15,680
I need to make you chai tea.

164
00:07:16,280 --> 00:07:20,700
Now, I have all the ingredients except cardamom seeds.

165
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:24,010
Do you happen to have any on you?

166
00:07:25,100 --> 00:07:28,060
Sorry, I left them in my turban.

167
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:32,610
Oh, I'll make English breakfast tea.

168
00:07:32,610 --> 00:07:33,830
They destroyed your culture.

169
00:07:33,830 --> 00:07:35,650
That's close enough.

170
00:07:38,550 --> 00:07:41,180
You know, I'm curious,

171
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:44,660
why are you so upset about seeing Emily with another man?

172
00:07:44,660 --> 00:07:47,170
Wouldn't you be upset if you saw Amy out with someone else?

173
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:48,150
Can't happen.

174
00:07:48,150 --> 00:07:50,790
We have an ironclad relationship agreement

175
00:07:50,790 --> 00:07:52,930
which precludes her from physical contact

176
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:54,990
with anyone other than me.

177
00:07:55,880 --> 00:07:58,300
But you don't have sex with her, either.

178
00:07:58,780 --> 00:08:00,410
Slick, huh?

179
00:08:01,990 --> 00:08:04,400
To be truthful, Emily and I haven't dated that long,

180
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:06,580
and we never agreed to be exclusive to each other.

181
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:08,210
Have you had intercourse?

182
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:09,100
No.

183
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:10,540
Well, stick to your guns.

184
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:12,550
There will be a lot of pressure.

185
00:08:18,060 --> 00:08:20,640
I'm hungry again!

186
00:08:22,840 --> 00:08:25,820
It's like the world's fattest cuckoo clock.

187
00:08:29,960 --> 00:08:32,410
You know, you're always talking about having a baby someday.

188
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:34,500
This is exactly what it's gonna be like.

189
00:08:34,910 --> 00:08:36,060
No, it's not.

190
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:38,890
Come on. The constant fussing, eating, pooping,

191
00:08:38,890 --> 00:08:40,370
burping, drooling.

192
00:08:40,370 --> 00:08:41,460
We're even waiting for the day

193
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:43,920
when she can finally walk on her own.

194
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:45,860
Maybe you're right.

195
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:49,160
Anything she finds on the floor goes right in her mouth.

196
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:56,450
I'm just telling you now, if we do have kids,

197
00:08:56,450 --> 00:08:58,600
don't expect me to do all the work.

198
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:02,300
Hey, I'm a very paternal person.

199
00:09:02,300 --> 00:09:05,370
I'd be excellent at taking care of a baby.

200
00:09:05,370 --> 00:09:07,810
I'm still hungry!

201
00:09:07,810 --> 00:09:09,940
I'm coming, you big baby!

202
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:17,330
You know, the only thing worse than doing a movie

203
00:09:17,330 --> 00:09:19,380
where they glue monkey hair to your ass

204
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:20,810
is getting fired from a movie

205
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,510
where they glue monkey hair to your ass.

206
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:27,240
Forget it, man, it's crap.

207
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,840
You just move on to the next thing.

208
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:30,250
Yeah, well, it's easy for you to say.

209
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:32,140
You used to be famous.

210
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:35,530
Hey. I just lost a job for you.

211
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:38,110
You're right, I'm sorry, you're famous.

212
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:40,780
Penny, it's not about being famous.

213
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,570
It's about the art.

214
00:09:42,570 --> 00:09:45,180
It's about the passion we have for our craft.

215
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:49,550
I have an audition for Sharknado 2!

216
00:09:49,970 --> 00:09:52,660
If I book this, I am totally gonna pay you back for this beer.

217
00:09:56,380 --> 00:09:58,950
God, what am I doing with my life?

218
00:09:58,950 --> 00:10:00,880
You having second thoughts about acting?

219
00:10:00,880 --> 00:10:02,810
You were on set, you saw what it was like.

220
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:05,060
Yeah, but it's not always that bad.

221
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,340
Oh, really?

222
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,700
What about when you did, uh,

223
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:09,670
Anne Frank at that cute little theater?

224
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:12,100
It was over a bowling alley.

225
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:14,370
Yeah, but...

226
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:17,230
there was ample parking.

227
00:10:18,680 --> 00:10:19,760
Are you done?

228
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,230
And you were so good in the TV commercial.

229
00:10:22,230 --> 00:10:24,800
It was for hemorrhoid cream.

230
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:28,840
And I got itchy and swollen just watching you.

231
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:34,290
Leonard, you are really not cheering me up.

232
00:10:34,290 --> 00:10:35,200
Come on.

233
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,690
How can you be sad when you're going home

234
00:10:36,690 --> 00:10:39,180
with all five-foot-six of this?

235
00:10:40,650 --> 00:10:43,590
You think you're five-foot-six, that's funny.

236
00:10:47,010 --> 00:10:48,530
I don't understand it.

237
00:10:48,530 --> 00:10:49,720
I'm a nice guy,

238
00:10:50,060 --> 00:10:51,230
I have a great job,

239
00:10:51,230 --> 00:10:52,200
I'm well-educated,

240
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:54,040
come from a good family...

241
00:10:54,430 --> 00:10:56,860
Why don't women want to be with me?

242
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,930
An interesting question.

243
00:11:00,900 --> 00:11:02,130
Well...

244
00:11:02,130 --> 00:11:03,850
good night.

245
00:11:05,830 --> 00:11:07,050
Don't send me home.

246
00:11:07,050 --> 00:11:08,960
I can't be alone right now.

247
00:11:08,960 --> 00:11:10,530
That's your problem.

248
00:11:10,530 --> 00:11:12,150
You can't be alone.

249
00:11:12,150 --> 00:11:13,500
What do you mean?

250
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:18,170
How many women have you had dates with?

251
00:11:19,210 --> 00:11:20,480
Eleven.

252
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:21,930
How many of those women

253
00:11:21,930 --> 00:11:24,920
did you think would become your perfect companion?

254
00:11:26,050 --> 00:11:27,370
Eleven.

255
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:28,760
Wait.

256
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:30,710
Do I count the 200-pound Sailor Moon girl

257
00:11:30,710 --> 00:11:33,610
that Howard and I had a threesome with at Comic Con?

258
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:38,070
Sure.

259
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,060
I'll stick with 11.

260
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:42,590
She liked Howard better.

261
00:11:44,690 --> 00:11:47,280
Well, now do you see the problem?

262
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,120
Maybe.

263
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,210
I... I don't know.

264
00:11:51,210 --> 00:11:52,740
You... It's late, I-I should...

265
00:11:52,740 --> 00:11:53,960
I should go.

266
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,770
Look, I-I do get what you're saying.

267
00:12:00,770 --> 00:12:02,050
Instead of desperately clinging

268
00:12:02,050 --> 00:12:03,850
to any woman who will go out with me,

269
00:12:03,850 --> 00:12:06,550
I need to work on my fear of being alone.

270
00:12:07,410 --> 00:12:10,560
I was trying to suggest chemical castration, but...

271
00:12:13,180 --> 00:12:14,070
...it's my bedtime,

272
00:12:14,070 --> 00:12:16,660
so whatever gets you out the door. Good night.

273
00:12:21,060 --> 00:12:22,550
Howie, I'm back!

274
00:12:22,550 --> 00:12:24,960
Shh-shh-shh, I just got her to sleep.

275
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,920
Sorry.

276
00:12:25,920 --> 00:12:26,880
What took you so long?

277
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,620
The grocery store is a few blocks away.

278
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:29,940
They only had regular yogurt.

279
00:12:29,940 --> 00:12:31,010
I had to go to a different store

280
00:12:31,010 --> 00:12:33,880
to get the extra-fat kind your mom likes.

281
00:12:34,820 --> 00:12:37,090
Then why do I smell coffee on your breath?

282
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:38,040
So what?

283
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,490
After two days of taking care of her,

284
00:12:39,490 --> 00:12:41,680
excuse me for stopping to get a mocha.

285
00:12:41,680 --> 00:12:43,030
A mocha?

286
00:12:43,030 --> 00:12:45,890
Well, it must be nice to be queen.

287
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:47,280
Queen?

288
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:48,830
I've been killing myself here!

289
00:12:48,830 --> 00:12:49,730
Well, whose fault is that?

290
00:12:49,730 --> 00:12:51,160
I wanted to get a nurse, but you were all,

291
00:12:51,160 --> 00:12:54,940
"I'm nice. I want to take care of people."

292
00:12:56,560 --> 00:12:58,270
I'm glad I got that mocha.

293
00:12:58,270 --> 00:13:00,130
And you know what else I'm glad about?

294
00:13:00,130 --> 00:13:04,200
I bought you a brownie and I ate it in the car!

295
00:13:06,280 --> 00:13:08,900
Howard!

296
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:10,110
Thanks a lot.

297
00:13:10,110 --> 00:13:12,480
Now I have to go rub her belly again.

298
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,330
Thanks for letting me come over.

299
00:13:23,330 --> 00:13:23,920
Of course.

300
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:25,610
Please, come in.

301
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:28,640
I just wanted to say

302
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:31,040
how sorry I am about tonight, and...

303
00:13:31,040 --> 00:13:33,780
I want to make sure that we're okay.

304
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:35,500
Uh, look, you and I haven't made

305
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,500
- any commitments to each other. - I know.

306
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:39,730
I just felt like I needed to explain.

307
00:13:39,730 --> 00:13:41,470
The guy I was with did my last tattoo,

308
00:13:41,470 --> 00:13:43,280
and he's been asking me out for months.

309
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,630
I finally said yes just to get it over with.

310
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:47,310
It's okay.

311
00:13:47,310 --> 00:13:48,720
Really?

312
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:51,040
Well, I mean, yeah, it freaked me out a little,

313
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,980
but that's my issue, not yours.

314
00:13:56,050 --> 00:13:57,340
If I saw you out with another woman,

315
00:13:57,340 --> 00:13:59,230
I'd be pretty upset.

316
00:13:59,680 --> 00:14:01,120
Thank you.

317
00:14:03,170 --> 00:14:04,250
Not just for being upset,

318
00:14:04,250 --> 00:14:06,660
but for believing that could happen.

319
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:13,090
Just so you know, I'm not seeing anyone else.

320
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:15,260
Well, me, neither.

321
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,720
- Okay. - Okay.

322
00:14:18,050 --> 00:14:18,900
Please.

323
00:14:18,900 --> 00:14:22,190
So, uh... you... you have tattoos?

324
00:14:22,190 --> 00:14:24,460
- Yeah. - I don't.

325
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:26,860
I have a hole in my belly button

326
00:14:26,860 --> 00:14:29,100
that may or may not have been a piercing.

327
00:14:30,110 --> 00:14:31,190
That's cool.

328
00:14:31,190 --> 00:14:32,940
It's a piercing.

329
00:14:34,650 --> 00:14:35,530
So, uh...

330
00:14:35,530 --> 00:14:36,920
how many tattoos?

331
00:14:37,410 --> 00:14:38,950
One on my shoulder,

332
00:14:38,950 --> 00:14:40,410
one not on my shoulder

333
00:14:40,410 --> 00:14:44,650
and one really not on my shoulder.

334
00:14:46,040 --> 00:14:47,270
It's, uh...

335
00:14:47,270 --> 00:14:49,940
been a long time since I've seen a girl's...

336
00:14:49,940 --> 00:14:52,270
really not her shoulder.

337
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:57,780
Well...how about you show me your piercing

338
00:14:57,780 --> 00:15:01,120
and I show you my tattoos?

339
00:15:06,590 --> 00:15:08,000
But, uh, before I take my shirt off,

340
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:11,230
I just need like ten minutes to do some crunches.

341
00:15:17,230 --> 00:15:19,230
Oh, my God.

342
00:15:19,230 --> 00:15:21,430
What a day.

343
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,280
Can I get you anything?

344
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:25,290
No.

345
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:28,770
I need to start making some smart decisions.

346
00:15:29,150 --> 00:15:30,420
With your career?

347
00:15:30,420 --> 00:15:32,300
With my life.

348
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:33,870
Like what?

349
00:15:34,290 --> 00:15:36,100
I don't know.

350
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:38,970
We could get married.

351
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:40,420
Come on, be serious.

352
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,780
I am.

353
00:15:42,510 --> 00:15:43,670
Why?

354
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:46,310
Because I'm a-a "smart decision"?

355
00:15:46,310 --> 00:15:47,980
Well, yeah.

356
00:15:47,980 --> 00:15:51,800
So I'm like a bran muffin.

357
00:15:53,030 --> 00:15:54,300
What...No, that's not what I'm saying.

358
00:15:54,300 --> 00:15:55,420
No, it's exactly what you're saying.

359
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:57,200
I'm the boring thing you're choosing

360
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,530
because I'm good for you.

361
00:15:58,530 --> 00:15:59,330
What does it matter?

362
00:15:59,330 --> 00:16:00,960
The point is, I'm choosing you.

363
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,280
Well, it matters a lot!

364
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:04,340
I don't want to be a bran muffin.

365
00:16:04,340 --> 00:16:06,120
I-I want to be a...

366
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,990
Cinnabon, you know?

367
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:11,610
A strawberry Pop-Tart.

368
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:13,070
Something you're excited about

369
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:15,910
even though it could give you diabetes.

370
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:19,270
Sweetie, you can be any pastry you want.

371
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:21,030
No, no. No, it's too late.

372
00:16:21,030 --> 00:16:22,320
I-I'm your bran muffin.

373
00:16:22,320 --> 00:16:25,370
Probably fat-free and good for your colon.

374
00:16:26,810 --> 00:16:27,700
You know what? Forget it.

375
00:16:27,700 --> 00:16:28,980
I never should've brought it up.

376
00:16:29,430 --> 00:16:31,490
You know I want to marry you,

377
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:33,280
but you're only doing this because you got fired

378
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:35,010
and you're feeling sorry for yourself.

379
00:16:35,010 --> 00:16:37,400
Okay, it may look that way, but getting fired from that movie

380
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:39,030
was the best thing that could have happened to me, okay?

381
00:16:39,030 --> 00:16:41,480
I finally realize I don't need to be famous

382
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:43,330
or have some big career to be happy.

383
00:16:43,330 --> 00:16:44,530
Then what do you need?

384
00:16:44,530 --> 00:16:47,080
You, you stupid pop-tart!

385
00:16:55,630 --> 00:16:57,770
Then I guess I'm in.

386
00:16:59,190 --> 00:16:59,880
Really?

387
00:16:59,880 --> 00:17:01,970
You "guess you're in"?

388
00:17:02,780 --> 00:17:04,130
Not like, "I guess I'm in."

389
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:06,900
Like "I guess... I'm in!"

390
00:17:08,450 --> 00:17:09,700
Okay.

391
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,060
Cool.

392
00:17:15,190 --> 00:17:16,350
So is that it?

393
00:17:16,350 --> 00:17:18,540
Are... are we engaged?

394
00:17:18,540 --> 00:17:20,360
Yeah, I think so.

395
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:24,080
All right.

396
00:17:26,550 --> 00:17:28,010
What's wrong?

397
00:17:28,420 --> 00:17:29,320
I'm not sure.

398
00:17:29,320 --> 00:17:32,820
Just... feels a little anticlimactic.

399
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:36,450
Yeah, it kind of does, huh?

400
00:17:37,850 --> 00:17:40,180
Oh, I know.

401
00:17:41,300 --> 00:17:43,200
This might help.

402
00:17:48,230 --> 00:17:50,040
Where did you get a ring?

403
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,710
I've...

404
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:53,870
had it for a couple years, not important.

405
00:17:58,900 --> 00:18:00,460
Penny...

406
00:18:00,460 --> 00:18:02,740
will you marry me?

407
00:18:03,640 --> 00:18:05,470
Oh, my God, yes.

408
00:18:09,380 --> 00:18:10,850
This would have been so much more romantic

409
00:18:10,850 --> 00:18:13,490
if you didn't have monkey hair on your finger.

410
00:18:22,930 --> 00:18:24,400
How you feeling?

411
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:26,230
Last night was a little rough,

412
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:28,800
but I think we're gonna get through this.

413
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:30,100
I'm proud of us.

414
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:31,970
Me, too.

415
00:18:31,970 --> 00:18:34,210
Where's my pancakes?!

416
00:18:34,210 --> 00:18:37,270
Coming, Mrs. Wolowitz!

417
00:18:42,450 --> 00:18:43,780
You were right.

418
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:46,150
Welcome to Team Putz.

